        <section style="-uslm-dtd:section" identifier="/us/sComp/116/7/s10" styleType="OLC">
            <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="10">SEC. 10. </num><heading style="-uslm-dtd:header">RELATIONSHIP TO FEDERAL AGENCIES. </heading>
            <content style="-uslm-dtd:text" class="block">Section 70909 of title 36, United States Code, is amended to read as follows:<quotedContent style="-uslm-dtd:quoted-block">
            <section style="-uslm-dtd:section" styleType="USC">
                <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="70909">“§ 70909. </num><heading style="-uslm-dtd:header">RELATIONSHIP TO FEDERAL AGENCIES </heading>
                <subsection style="-uslm-dtd:subsection" styleType="OLC">
                    <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="a">“(a) </num><heading style="-uslm-dtd:header">In General.—</heading><content style="-uslm-dtd:text">On request of the board of directors, the FFA may collaborate with Federal agencies, including the Department of Education and the Department of Agriculture on matters of mutual interest and benefit.</content>
                </subsection>
                <subsection style="-uslm-dtd:subsection" styleType="OLC">
                    <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="b">“(b) </num><heading style="-uslm-dtd:header">Agency Assistance.—</heading><content style="-uslm-dtd:text">Those Federal agencies may make personnel, services, and facilities available to administer or assist in the administration of the activities of the FFA.</content>
                </subsection>
                <subsection style="-uslm-dtd:subsection" styleType="OLC">
                    <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="c">“(c) </num><heading style="-uslm-dtd:header">Agency Compensation.—</heading><content style="-uslm-dtd:text">Personnel of the Federal agencies may not receive compensation from the FFA for their services, except that travel and other legitimate expenses as defined by the Federal agencies and approved by the board may be paid.</content>
                </subsection>
                <subsection style="-uslm-dtd:subsection" styleType="OLC">
                    <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="d">“(d) </num><heading style="-uslm-dtd:header">Cooperation With State Boards.—</heading><content style="-uslm-dtd:text">The Federal agencies also may cooperate with State boards and other organizations for career and technical education to assist in the promotion of activities of the FFA.”</content>
                </subsection>
            </section></quotedContent>.</content>
        </section>
        <section style="-uslm-dtd:section" identifier="/us/sComp/116/7/s11" styleType="OLC">
            <num style="-uslm-dtd:enum" value="11">SEC. 11. </num><heading style="-uslm-dtd:header">HEADQUARTERS AND PRINCIPAL OFFICE. </heading>
            <content style="-uslm-dtd:text" class="block">Section 70910 of title 36, United States Code, is amended by striking “<quotedText style="-uslm-dtd:quote">of the corporation shall be in the District of Columbia. However, the activities of the corporation are not confined to the District of Columbia but</quotedText>” and inserting “<quotedText style="-uslm-dtd:quote">of the FFA shall be as provided in the constitution or bylaws of the FFA. The activities of the FFA</quotedText>”.</content>
